=== NATURE OF THE SOURCE (presentational; states disposition) ===
  LoadingSkeleton is a *presentational* component: the web source fetches nothing
  (its only deps are @/components/ui GlassPanel, @/components/feedback Skeleton,
  @/components/motion FadeIn). It IS the loading-phase chrome the cost-analysis
  parent (web `useCostAnalysisData`) renders while its query is in flight, so the
  remote envelope (empty / error / stale / offline) belongs to that PARENT, not to
  the skeleton — identical disposition to the 0076 HighlightCard / ToolCard
  presentational surfaces (documented verbatim in LoadingSkeleton.Model.swift).
  The branches the web source DOES own are reproduced + tested here:
    • responsive layout — the Tailwind grid breakpoints (`flex-col sm:flex-row`,
      `grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-6`, `grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2`),
      ported pure as LoadingSkeletonLayout (same seam as 0048 SummaryStatsRow),
      measured via the iOS-18/macOS-15 `onGeometryChange` width hook, and
    • the fixed shape of every shimmer region (header title/subtitle/action, the
      six stat-card lines, the two chart blocks, the five table rows) — each
      `<Skeleton>` width+height taken verbatim from the web source.

