=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources: NONE (web "Data sources: (none — pure presentational component)").
    No HTTP, no store — nothing to bind; documented, not narrowed.
  - Composition (web FadeIn > space-y-6 p-6 column):
      • FadeIn          -> TSFadeIn (shared motion parity; honors Reduce Motion).
      • Header          -> title 220x28 + subtitle 340x16 (TSSkeleton) + a 200x36
                           pill action; `flex-col` stacked < sm, `sm:flex-row`
                           justify-between >= 640 (LoadingSkeletonLayout.headerIsHorizontal).
      • Stat-card grid  -> 6x TSGlassPanel, each three lines (60%x14, 80%x24 mt-2,
                           40%x12 mt-1); cols 2 / lg:3 / xl:6 (cardColumnCount).
      • Chart row       -> 2x TSGlassPanel, title 40%x16 + body 200 (mt-4); cols
                           1 / lg:2 (chartColumnCount).
      • Table block     -> TSGlassPanel, title 30%x16 + five 32-tall rows (space-y-2).
    Tailwind px gaps mapped to design tokens (gap-4/space-y-6 -> lg/x2xl, mt-2/mt-1
    -> sm/xs). Fixed-px header bars cap to the measured content width so they never
    overflow a narrow phone; percentage bars measure their container (GeometryReader)
    so "60%/80%/40%/30%" stay faithful at any column width.
  - States: the surface IS the loading state; every region renders (no hidden
    surface). The remote envelope (empty/error/stale/offline) is the cost-analysis
    parent's responsibility (presentational disposition above) — reproduced there,
    not duplicated here.
  - i18n (P1/S10): web renders no visible copy (pure shimmer), so there are no web
    t() keys to preserve. The one native string is the consolidated VoiceOver
    "Loading…" label (loadingSkeleton.a11y.loading), declared in LoadingSkeleton.strings
    + resolved via LoadingSkeletonStrings; NO English literals in native code.
  - Accessibility: each TSSkeleton bar is accessibilityHidden; the surface exposes
    ONE combined label ("Loading…") with .updatesFrequently so VoiceOver announces
    progress instead of silence. Dynamic Type (system fonts via the shared
    components), Reduce Motion (TSSkeleton shimmer + TSFadeIn) honored.
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): the view's `.task` calls LoadingSkeletonSurface.reportOpen,
    emitting view.opened with surface slug "LoadingSkeleton" (OSLog default; prod
    app injects the shared diagnostics adapter). Slug asserted in tests.

